Now, we could be tempted to hit F5 and try it out... However, if we were to do that,
we would face a rather disappointing outcome, as shown in the following screenshot:
The reason for this is quite obvious: even if we're running multiple checks, we're still
relying on the default outcome message... which is nothing more than a Boolean sum
of the statuses returned by all the checked hosts. For that very reason, if at least one of
them is Unhealthy, the whole check will be flagged as Unhealthy as well.
